{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1165754-question-about-nephandi","id":1165754,"title":"Question about Nephandi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-06T20:22:31-08:00","id":1165754,"title":"Question about Nephandi","content":"<span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">HOW SUBTIL are nephandi? . i meant, when it comes to fighting a nephandi what its expected. Would one of them pull a fucking machine gun on your arse, or its it expected for him to throw objects with his mind or grow tentacles? because i know nephandi are NOT paradox Proof </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T21:25:46-08:00","id":1165765,"title":"","content":"The Nephandi can be very subtle, but it depends on the individual. The blatant ones don't last long, but the subtle Nephandi can corrupt Sleepers, institutions, spirits, Tradition mages, Technocrats, Disparates, anyone.<br /> <br /> If you're fighting a blatant Nephandi expect any kind of twisted, messed up magic. If you're fighting a subtle Nephandi you can make that an entire campaign where the PC's find hints of the Nephandic corruption, trace it back to its source, and eventually confront the Fallen One directly. They also like to keep the Ascension War going, as it distracts the Traditions and Technocracy from their plans while also being a form of corruption in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:09:33-08:00","id":1165813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1165754-question-about-nephandi#post1165754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> HOW SUBTIL are nephandi?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi can be, and often are subtle to such an extent, that most True Mages don't realize at all that they are speaking to or interacting with a True Mage who is a Nephandus; the subtlety and secrecy is maintained even when True Mages (of the Traditions, for example) are interacting with the Nephandus (or two or more Nephandi) over a long period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-07-2017, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T06:14:23-08:00","id":1165842,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but in the context of this question:<br /> <br /> A Nephandus can be as subtle or blatant as she wants to avoid Paradox . There's no restriction other than her Paradigm, which it's whatever Paradigm she had before falling. That Paradigm more than her &quot;faction&quot; it's what determines which kind of effect she summons.<br /> <br /> Hence, if you face the Nephandi in their lairs of evil where they summon the eldrich abominatons (probably a Sanctum) you may eat more tentacles than out in the street. Much like with any other mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:50:32-08:00","id":1165938,"title":"","content":"It seems worth noting that it is a standard Nephandi tactic to use blatant &quot;bad&quot; mages (whether they've gone through the Cauls or not) to keep other mages busy and off their scent; if not ingratiate themselves.<br /> <br /> However subtle or vulgar a Nephandus' magic might be, the smart ones keep it well hidden from other mages, and make sure someone blatant is around to keep their enemies busy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T04:34:45-08:00","id":1166055,"title":"","content":"personally i think a good part of the nephandi conscripts are high school dropout jocks who decided to enter this caul-thing to break some stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T13:34:19-08:00","id":1166155,"title":"","content":"Nephandi are usually really, really subtle in their actions and they always attempt to turn every situation at their advantage without showing their hand.<br /> That said, if they come down to a fight and they can't manipulate it and persuade people to defend them, Nephandi fight like every other mage: coincidental effects are easier, safer and better, why should they pull paradox over themselves? Of course, if we're talking about the Umbra or reality zones maybe there are vulgar effects they can get by with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 12-09-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T17:47:01-08:00","id":1166207,"title":"","content":"First, we need to define &quot;SUBTIL [sic]&quot;. Either we mean subtle in the general sense of not wanting to attract attention, or subtle in the sense of Coincidental.<br /> <br /> In the former case, Nephandi last longest when they attract as little attention as possible. These are the folks who prefer to work through intermediaries, with intermediaries for their intermediaries. A safe and secure Nephandus is one as many layers removed from their pawns as possible, so nothing can be traced to them. If they have to make a personal appearance - like as the hidden master of one of the infernal cults they established or co-opted - it will be in some magickal or mundane disguise, or even remotely through an illusion or possessed flunky.<br /> <br /> For the record, because of the unique nature of Nephandi priorities - that is, Evil For Evil's Sake - they have a wide latitude for what constitutes a &quot;Win&quot; condition. So long as chaos, mistrust, death, and suffering are furthered, a Nephandus gives not one damn about how it gets there. Consider the Trope Xanatos Gambit, for the kinds of &quot;Even if I lose, I Win&quot; tactics a Nephandus can utilize because of this.<br /> <br /> If a Nephandus is cornered or needs to get their hands dirty, they'll use whatever means can get the job done, while also not attracting attention to themselves. A gun is more likely to attract attention than a knife, but that same gun is much more subtle than opening a gate to the far realms and letting tentacled horrors reach through to strangle people. Needs must, and a machine gun is at least normal in the mortal criminal underworld (and, sadly, used more and more often by the unhinged, even in mundane settings).<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of magick, that brings us to our next point. Put simply, Nephandi are no more immune to the effects of Paradox as any other Mage, save the Marauders. Some are more easily slotted into the Consensus than others, but the rules of Paradox still apply. As such, Nephandi will hew towards Coincidence wherever possible, unless they have a reason (or desire) to cut loose. Like any mage, a Nephandus may happen to really want to burn someone alive with their full magickal might, and will do so from time to time. If, that is, they think they can get away with it. Risk/Reward comes into play, as does the character's magickal specialty. Sometimes the feats an Awakened person (even a Fallen one) are expert in just don't play well with Reality. They have to make the choice over whether they'll employ those feats, or settle for something more Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T20:56:15-08:00","id":1167829,"title":"","content":"any ingame examples of their rotes or how subtle can they be, or how do they hide their resonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T18:28:51-08:00","id":1168076,"title":"","content":"There are few specific rotes to them. It is not a Paradigm, but an allegiance. To play a Nephandus, start with any other Paradigm and just make the character &quot;evil for evil's sake&quot;.<br /> <br /> What will distinguish them isn't the rotes they have access to, but the lack of ethics to do something, magical or mundane, and the weakening and eventual destruction of the world as the only true goal. This also means they are more likely than most to mix alien practices with their original Paradigm, but they follow no special rule on this. At most, they will favor themes of corruption, nihilism and/or demonology.<br /> <br /> It isn't in their ways, just in their goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T19:28:25-08:00","id":1169801,"title":"","content":"I've had a Nephandus in my chronicle from day 1 of the game. He worked closely with one of the main characters (the PC had a club and was a performer, the Nephandus was a promoter). The game started about 4 years ago, and 2 weeks ago they discovered his true identity, even as he was leaving a trail of bodies over time (had the players paid closer attention, they would have found his pattern much earlier). It's the goal of a leading Nephadus to never be noticed, never be caught. Thus, subtlety is key. I took it for granted that this very old Nephandus had a way of concealing his diabolical nature. In fact, he's body swapped several times over the centuries and is in the top 3 of most powerful mages in my New York City game.<br /> <br /> The OP kind of answered his own question. Nephandi tend to draw Paradox through enactment of their higher end rituals. In combat, things would only get worse. So yeah, as has been mentioned, Nephandi tend to use underlings, pawns and thralls to keep the heat off or at least provide time for escape. If they must fight....well, it depends <i>entirely </i>on the situation: how strong is the Nephandus, what is his Paradigm, how many opponents and what does he know of them, has he minions to assist, etc. <br /> <br /> In my case, the Nephandus owned a hotel. Within its walls he trapped the ghosts of all those he killed (going back several centuries), most of which had become ravenous spectres in the meantime. A Hollow One necromancer passing by the hotel sensed something, investigated, and had her soul rapidly destroyed and her body moved by the Nephandus, who'd been thrown out of his comfort zone by the intrusion. She was found quickly, the PC's got involved, the Traditions called a Code Black, bringing in the Technocracy, and--long session short--defeated the Nephandus...almost, as he has hopped into another body. Next session, the players will get a hint as to who that is (the Nephandus has to have prepared the person ahead of time).<br /> <br /> So that's one way to go about it. Cheers~<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}